  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The number of ways in which&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math>&nbsp;distinct balls can be distributed among&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;boxes is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></msup></math></p><p>The number of ways in which&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;contains&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;balls is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>9</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></math></p><p>Using the classical definition of probability we can say the required probability <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>9</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>9</mn></mmultiscripts><mn>27</mn></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>9</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>28</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>9</mn></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>28</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>11</mn></math></p><p>Now, consider&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>|</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;satisfies&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>|</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>"
